    "causal_summary": "The note database fork's native Excel-style formula engine already evaluates `IF`, exposes `Math` on the sandbox eval scope (`ComputedField.ts:433-437`), and already dual-names `POWER`/`POW` — but Notion's `ifs(cond, val, ..., [else])` branch chain is absent (users must hand-nest `IF`), and the common Excel-style math names `SQRT` / `LN` / `LOG10` / `EXP` / `CBRT` are missing even though raw `Math.` works",
